PROVENANCE

The files in this directory and below it are a program of the nofib benchmark suite (the collection
of Haskell programs that Will Partain gathered at Glasgow), which jhc, John Meacham's Haskell
compiler, keeps among its regression tests, regress/tests/9_nofib in its repository. Its directory
names nofib; the program is a variant of nofib's imaginary/primes (compared with that file at
nofib's commit f34b90b5a6ce46284693119a06d1133908b11856: the imports differ, and the_filter is
written out by hand).

They are vendored here without a licence, under the rule of this repository's owner, quoted:

    "If you want to vendor code without a license add a PROVENANCE alongside it instead."

rhc, the Haskell 98 compiler of this repository, compiles and runs them in its tests
(tests/hs/corpus: the programs of D56 of the haskell98 roadmap, which tests/hs/corpus/licences.tsv
lists with this file as their notice).

